            "review_title": "Review at Phuong Cua Seafood",
            "review_text": "Mervyn33\nSingapore, Singapore353 contributions\n0\nGood and Affordable Seafood in HCMC\nDec 2023 • Friends\nAlthough this seafood restaurant is not in the heart of the city .. it is 30 minutes drive from Ben Thanh Market to this Seafood restaurant by the river.\nNot an up market kind of settings or layout, more to the local style seafood restaurant.\n\nOne need to k ow the drills or ordering here .. after getting a table, you will be given a table number, with the table number then one will proceed to select or pick the live seafood that you want to have .. weight them and decide how you want it to be cooked. I think about 10 different way of cookings.\n\nWe have 5 female crabs .. cooked in two version .. one Curry Crab version and the other cooked with tamarind sauce. We had some steamed Squid with Spring Onions, Cheese Oysters, BBQ prawns, Clams two variations, Cockles - big and small varieties, some green vegetables, Vietnamese spring rolls and Salted fish fried rice, fried chicken .. and lots of beers.\nPrice wise it is indeed cheaper than those Seafood restaurant in the heart of HCMC that we had tried. The crabs were the main highlight and crabs with roe. Definitely the place to go for good crabs and cooking styles. I would recommend it.\nRead more\nWritten December 7, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
