            "review_text": "lovesweets2\nAvalon Beach, Australia497 contributions\n1\nMust not miss!!!\nMay 2017 • Couples\nThis is close to our apt, within 5 mins walk from saigon domaine and was recommended by an expat so we decided to try. I was worried on minimal reviews on TA and after we have been to this place, i understood why. 99.9% of the customers were vietnamese! The place was packed and we were the only foreigners there.. vietnam's best kept secret No More!\n\nThis is the place to go for cheap crab dish (around 250k vnd per kilo.. depending on how you want the crab cooked - steam, fried, curry..). We had been there twice and ordered bbq prawns, 1 kilo crab (fried n salted), grilled porkchops, 2 beers and strongbow within 510k-650k vnd.\n\nThe menu is in English and the staff speak very little to no english. Oftentimes we resorted to pointing what we want from the menu or use google translate! \n\nHere are some tips:\n1. When ordering crabs, you will have to goto an area to select your crab, weigh this and let the person in charge know ypu you'd like it to be cooked (menu on a board). He will then give you a printout showing how much the crab weighed n how much. You will need to show this your waiter/tress so they know to pick this up from their massive kitchen \n2. Just find a vacant table where you'd like to sit and a staff will come and give you the menu. The staff has their \"sections\". There wont be anyone to escort you to a table as you come in. \n3. Best come prepared with google translate or translations that will assist you in communicating. Staff are patient and will try their best to serve\n4. Wet towellete is extra charge of 2k vnd per. \n5. They may put some crackers on you table that you may think is for free. They are not! Took as an experience to learn. So dont touch unless you want to be charge.\n\nA definite must try!\nRead more\nWritten May 17, 2017",
